section#stemdeck.dark
  div
    h2 StemDeck × A³ Motion
    p.subline Four stems, four paths through the room, one beat.
    p
      | A moving stereo mix moves everything at once. StemDeck plays every track as
      | four stems and sends each on its own channel into A³ Core, where A³ Motion
      | moves them one by one: the drums hold the floor, the vocal circles overhead,
      | the synths breathe from wall to wall. And because StemDeck can be the tempo
      | master, every movement lands on the track's own beat.

    //- IMAGE: A³ Motion's sphere with four blobs on four different clips while StemDeck plays one track — drums, bass, other and vocals each in its own place
    //- GIF (short loop): a vocal stem taking off overhead while the drums stay put, StemDeck's stem meters beside A³ Motion's channel row

    .flex-container
      .stem
        p.channel ch 1
        h3 drums
        p hold the floor, or jump on the beat
      .stem
        p.channel ch 2
        h3 bass
        p stays put, where bass is happiest
      .stem
        p.channel ch 3
        h3 other
        p pads and synths, wall to wall
      .stem
        p.channel ch 4
        h3 vocals
        p over the heads of the crowd

    ul
      li two decks of four stems, split from any stereo track
      li each stem on its own A³ channel, moved on its own clip
      li StemDeck as Pro DJ Link tempo master — no CDJs needed
      li beat-synced movements, counted in bars

    a.more(href="https://a3-audio.github.io/a3-doc/user/stemdeck-with-motion.html") How to set it up
